    "updated_at": "2023-04-05T06:06:57Z",
    "body": "I was hoping that we could just require the underlying source to do cleanup in this case. But the underlying source doesn't know it is being used in async iteration. If it was being read from by a normal reader or a pipe then the rejected promise would not trigger cancellation.\r\n\r\nSo my current impression is that your solution is correct.",
